{"uncertainty": 0.2, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause of the failing uart_tx regression test: hold register reloaded while a frame is in flight", "summary": "Conclusion: rtl_bug. The defect is in the approved RTL under investigation [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1].\n\nDefect: the always block contains an unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;` placed before the `case (state)`. It runs in every state, not only in IDLE. The IDLE branch already loads `hold` when a frame starts, so this extra statement only changes behaviour in START, DATA and STOP.\n\nIncorrectness: the file's own header specifies 8N1 framing and says \"A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.\" A start pulse while busy overwrites `hold`. The frame still in progress then picks up its remaining bits from the new byte through `tx <= hold[bit_idx + 3'd1]`.\n\nCausality: the fault is written into `hold` in the cycle of the mid-frame start pulse. It becomes visible later, when each following data bit is serialised from the corrupted `hold`. The failing check marks where a corrupted bit was sampled, not the cycle where `hold` was overwritten. The state machine itself correctly ignores the pulse: no second frame is started and `busy` stays asserted. Only the payload is corrupted.\n\nObserved failure: triage reproduced the failure deterministically, with 1 of 4 checks failing and $finish reached at time 546000 [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2] [run:run-0002]. VeriTriage's top hypothesis was \"Likely RTL bug\", but only at 30% confidence with an unknown_failure classification [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. I treated that hypothesis as one candidate among four, not as a conclusion.\n\nRanked hypotheses, with the evidence that would refute each:\n\n(1) RTL bug: hold is reloaded while busy. This is the leading hypothesis, supported by reading the source against its own header clause.\n- It would be refuted if a frame with a mid-frame start pulse carrying different data were received intact.\n- The repro testbench uart_tx_rootcause_tb.v tests exactly this. Frame B sends 0x5A and pulses start with 0xFF during data bit 2. Bits 5 and 7 of 0x5A are 0, so the reload must flip them on this RTL.\n\n(2) Testbench bug: a wrong expectation in the regression check. Rejected as the primary cause.\n- The expected value in the new repro comes from the header specification (the byte presented at the accepted start, serialised LSB-first), not from RTL output.\n- Two control frames (0xA5 and 0x3C, with no mid-frame pulse) use the same receiver and the same checks. They are expected to pass, so a broken receiver or a wrong bit-order assumption would show up there.\n- It would be refuted further by the same testbench passing on the clean reference RTL, which I cannot observe here.\n\n(3) Infrastructure. Rejected.\n- The triage run built, reached $finish and failed a single counted check rather than crashing or timing out [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2].\n- A deterministic single-check failure is not the signature of a tool or environment fault.\n- A clean rebuild that changes the outcome would refute this rejection.\n\n(4) Spec ambiguity. Rejected.\n- The clause \"A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored\" explicitly fixes the behaviour under test in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1].\n- Ignoring a pulse cannot reasonably include adopting its data into the current frame.\n\nLimits:\n- I did not have the content of the triage testbench or of regression_fail.log. So I cannot confirm that its one failing check is the mid-frame reload scenario, rather than a different symptom of the same cause.\n- Recommended fix, for a later task and not done here: delete the unconditional pre-case `if (start) hold <= data;` and leave the IDLE-branch load as the only write to hold.\n- Recommended follow-up: an assertion that `hold` is stable while `busy` is asserted.\n\nRequirement served: [requirement:req-d10c4df532]."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/uart_tx_rootcause_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse while busy must not change the frame in flight", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the defect in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1], serving [requirement:req-d10c4df532].\n\nWhat it does:\n- Resets the DUT with CLKS_PER_BIT=4.\n- Sends control frame A (0xA5) and checks the received byte and the stop bit.\n- Sends frame B (0x5A) and pulses start with 0xFF while busy during data bit 2. It checks that busy was high at the pulse, that the received byte is still 0x5A, the stop bit, and that no ghost frame follows.\n- Sends control frame C (0x3C) and checks the byte and the stop bit.\n\nExpected results are taken from the header specification, not from RTL output. On the RTL under investigation, the frame B payload check is expected to fail because hold is reloaded. On RTL that ignores the pulse, all checks are expected to pass.\n\nIt counts its checks and prints exactly one `NIRMAAN-SIM <nonce> <passed> passed, <failed> failed` line just before $finish. A watchdog counts a timeout as a failed check and prints the same single verdict.", "entry": "uart_tx_rootcause_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run:run-0001", "run:run-0002"], "claims": ["The clean reference uart_tx presumably loads hold only in IDLE; I have not seen it, so the expectation that this repro passes on clean RTL is unverified.", "The triage testbench's single failing check is assumed to be a symptom of the same hold-reload defect; its content was not available to me.", "Frame B's mid-frame pulse with 0xFF is expected to flip received bits 5 and 7 (at least) on the RTL under investigation, causing the payload check to fail."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Outcome rtl_bug. The repro is built around the header clause 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored'. Control frames A and C guard against a receiver or expectation bug in the testbench itself. I have not run this testbench. The platform's simulator.run with expect=fail will decide whether it reproduces the failure on the approved RTL."}

=== FILE: tb/uart_tx_rootcause_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro for uart_tx: a start pulse while a frame is in flight must be ignored,
// so the frame in flight must still carry the byte accepted at its start.
// Expected values come from the specification (8N1, LSB first), not from RTL.
module uart_tx_rootcause_tb;
    localparam integer CPB = 4;

    reg        clk   = 1'b0;
    reg        rst   = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data  = 8'h00;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CPB)) dut (
        .clk(clk), .rst(rst), .start(start), .data(data), .tx(tx), .busy(busy)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    reg [7:0] rx_byte;
    reg       rx_stop;
    reg       busy_at_pulse;
    reg       ghost;
    integer   k;

    task check(input cond, input [8*40-1:0] name);
        begin
            if (cond) begin
                passed = passed + 1;
            end else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("CHECK FAILED: %0s at time %0t", name, $time);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task send(input [7:0] b);
        begin
            @(negedge clk);
            data  = b;
            start = 1'b1;
            @(negedge clk);
            start = 1'b0;
        end
    endtask

    // Samples the middle of every bit, starting from the start bit's falling edge.
    task receive(output [7:0] b, output s);
        integer i;
        begin
            @(negedge tx);
            repeat (CPB/2) @(posedge clk);
            #1;
            for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
                repeat (CPB) @(posedge clk);
                #1;
                b[i] = tx;
            end
            repeat (CPB) @(posedge clk);
            #1;
            s = tx;
        end
    endtask

    task finish_with_verdict;
        begin
            if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
                nonce = "none";
            $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
            $finish;
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        #200000;
        failed = failed + 1;
        $display("CHECK FAILED: watchdog timeout");
        finish_with_verdict;
    end

    initial begin
        repeat (4) @(posedge clk);
        @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(posedge clk);

        // Frame A: control frame, no interference.
        fork
            receive(rx_byte, rx_stop);
            send(8'hA5);
        join
        check(rx_byte == 8'hA5, "frame A payload 0xA5");
        check(rx_stop == 1'b1,  "frame A stop bit");
        wait (busy == 1'b0);
        repeat (CPB) @(posedge clk);

        // Frame B: start pulse with different data during data bit 2.
        fork
            receive(rx_byte, rx_stop);
            begin
                send(8'h5A);
                repeat (CPB*3) @(posedge clk);
                @(negedge clk);
                busy_at_pulse = busy;
                data  = 8'hFF;
                start = 1'b1;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0;
                data  = 8'h00;
            end
        join
        check(busy_at_pulse == 1'b1, "busy high at mid-frame pulse");
        check(rx_byte == 8'h5A, "frame B payload kept 0x5A");
        check(rx_stop == 1'b1,  "frame B stop bit");

        // The ignored pulse must not launch a second frame.
        wait (busy == 1'b0);
        ghost = 1'b0;
        for (k = 0; k < 3*CPB; k = k + 1) begin
            @(posedge clk);
            #1;
            if (busy !== 1'b0 || tx !== 1'b1)
                ghost = 1'b1;
        end
        check(ghost == 1'b0, "no frame from ignored pulse");

        // Frame C: control frame after the interference.
        fork
            receive(rx_byte, rx_stop);
            send(8'h3C);
        join
        check(rx_byte == 8'h3C, "frame C payload 0x3C");
        check(rx_stop == 1'b1,  "frame C stop bit");
        wait (busy == 1'b0);
        repeat (CPB) @(posedge clk);

        finish_with_verdict;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===

